Changes since v1.5.3:
	* Add direct untagged GeneralizedTime Rust BER/DER/CER roots for valid
	  explicitly zoned values under BER/CER-only selection. BER preserves raw
	  content; DER/CER normalize to UTC with bounded fractional precision and
	  strict CER prefix comparison. Document host-local C DER divergences.
	* Add direct untagged UTCTime Rust BER/DER/CER roots under BER/CER-only
	  selection. Preserve raw BER/DER content, normalize valid CER values to
	  seconds and Z using checked Gregorian arithmetic, reject noncanonical
	  CER framing, and compare generated C/Rust vectors and invalid inputs.
	* Extend direct Rust BER/DER/CER roots to the C-supported restricted
	  character strings under BER/CER-only selection. Preserve raw BER/DER
	  bytes, apply each C descriptor's CER repertoire or alignment rule,
	  share tag-4 CER fragmentation, and compare legacy UTF8, aliases,
	  malformed input, and resource boundaries with generated C.
	* Add direct untagged IA5String Rust BER/DER/CER support under
	  BER/CER-only selection. Preserve C-compatible raw BER and DER bytes,
	  apply the 7-bit repertoire for CER, and test OCTET STRING fragments,
	  canonical boundaries, malformed input, limits, and C interoperability.
	* Add direct untagged OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID Rust
	  BER/DER/CER roots under BER/CER-only selection. Retain arbitrarily
	  large subidentifiers as canonical base-128 content, check malformed
	  arcs and resource limits, and compare strict CER with C vectors.
	* Extend generated Rust BER/DER/CER support to untagged, unconstrained
	  top-level BIT STRING and OCTET STRING under BER/CER-only selection.
	  Compare C and Rust at CER fragment boundaries, check constructed BER
	  input and resource limits, and reject unsupported schemas before output.
	* Add a bounded-operation arbitrary-precision Rust INTEGER representation
	  for untagged, unconstrained BER/DER/CER generation. Normalize signed
	  bytes, validate malformed BER lengths and tags, compare strict CER with
	  canonical output, and check wide C interoperability and resource limits.
	  Include the BER runtime modules in installed data and the parity design
	  in distributed documentation.
	* Extend the bounded Rust BER/DER/CER flat SET slice to one resolved
	  context-specific IMPLICIT root tag under BER/CER-only selection. Preserve
	  effective-tag output order, unordered BER input, and shared CER limits.
	* Add one context-specific IMPLICIT tag on a direct flat Rust SEQUENCE
	  root under BER/CER-only selection. Preserve the shared record budget,
	  accept C-compatible BER root aliases, and require canonical CER framing.
	* Add a bounded Rust BER/DER/CER inline SEQUENCE child in untagged SEQUENCE
	  and BER/CER-only SET records. Share record limits across parent and child,
	  support natural, IMPLICIT, and EXPLICIT child tags, and check nested EOCs,
	  output ordering, canonical CER, and aggregate scratch storage.
	* Avoid applying the parent EXPLICIT tag twice to inline generated C
	  ENUMERATED members. Add exact DER/CER SEQUENCE and SET vectors and
	  BER/CER decoding regressions with IMPLICIT and BOOLEAN controls.
	* Add one resolved context-specific EXPLICIT wrapper per direct member in
	  the bounded Rust BER/DER/CER flat SEQUENCE and SET slices. Validate the
	  intrinsic child and wrapper boundaries, canonical CER form, high tags,
	  malformed inputs, resource limits, and C interoperability.
	* Add resolved context-specific IMPLICIT member tags to the bounded Rust
	  BER/DER/CER flat SEQUENCE and SET slices, including automatic and high tag
	  numbers. Keep field kinds separate from effective identifiers, preserve
	  C-compatible BER aliases, and compare strict CER against canonical output.
	* Add a bounded Rust BER/DER/CER flat SET slice with unordered BER field
	  decoding, canonical tag-ordered DER/CER output, strict CER comparison,
	  OPTIONAL/default handling, and shared record resource accounting.
	  Compare generated C and Rust SET vectors and reject unsupported schemas.
	* Extend flat Rust BER/DER/CER SEQUENCE fields to direct ENUMERATED and
	  finite bounded BIT/OCTET STRING values. Keep constructed BER flattening,
	  CER fragmentation, and strict canonical comparison on one record budget;
	  add generated C comparisons at DER length and CER fragment boundaries.
	* Add generated Rust BER prefix decoding, DER encoding, CER encoding, and
	  strict CER decoding for flat untagged SEQUENCE records with unique direct
	  BOOLEAN, NULL, and bounded INTEGER fields. Support required, OPTIONAL,
	  literal BOOLEAN/INTEGER DEFAULT, and empty records with one shared resource
	  budget and generated C interoperability vectors.
	* Extend generated Rust BER decoding, DER encoding, CER encoding, and
	  strict CER decoding to direct nonextensible ENUMERATED and finite-size
	  BIT/OCTET STRING values. Add bounded constructed-string BER parsing,
	  CER fragmentation, C interoperability vectors, and malformed-input tests.
	  Record the architecture and remaining C parity work.
	* Free partially decoded APER SET members in the truncation regression test,
	  eliminating its LeakSanitizer failure in C/C++ CI and distcheck.
	* Fix issue #594 C XER output: separate SET members with one newline,
	  materialize absent DEFAULT members in basic as well as canonical XER,
	  and generate REAL DEFAULT callbacks for native and wide C storage.
	  Generated regressions cover SET and SEQUENCE XER plus JER REAL defaults.
	* Escape BMPString and UniversalString JER content as valid JSON and
	  flatten SEQUENCE extension-addition group members in JER objects.
	  Add malformed Unicode and generated group regressions.
	* Add opt-in Rust basic XER encoding for a bounded flat SET/SEQUENCE
	  subset, including issue #594 DEFAULT values, tag-ordered SET output,
	  XML escaping, C parity vectors, and strict resource limits.
	* Extend C CBOR SEQUENCE decoding with duplicate/required-member checks,
	  deferred direct selected OPEN TYPE resolution, and transactional output.
	  Flatten SET extension-group leaves into its repository-defined name-keyed
	  map, validate duplicate names, and preserve existing SET values on errors.
	* Validate C CBOR SEQUENCE OF and SET OF array counts, list storage, and child
	  consumption before accepting values; stage decoded lists so malformed
	  input preserves a preallocated value.
	* Validate C CBOR CHOICE descriptors and active arms before encoding, then
	  decode a complete one-entry map into staged storage with UTF-8 key and
	  full child-consumption checks. Add generated sanitizer and fuzz regressions.
	* Harden C CBOR byte strings, BIT STRING padding, negative large INTEGER
	  conversion, UTF-8 text and UTF8String validation, recursive unknown-item
	  skipping, and public codec argument validation. Add malformed-length,
	  CONTAINING, fuzz corpus, and preallocated-value regressions.
	* Expand opt-in Rust CBOR encoding and decoding for direct BIT/OCTET STRING,
	  flat SEQUENCE with OPTIONAL/default fields, narrow CHOICE alternatives,
	  selected OPEN TYPE, and typed primitive CONTAINING values. Add bounded map
	  parsing, C interoperability vectors, and unsupported-shape gates.
	* Add bounded C SET BER/DER direct OPEN TYPE support for one unambiguous
	  explicitly tagged member, with two-pass unordered decoding, canonical
	  DER sorting, selector checks, and generated sanitizer regressions.
	* Add a bounded C SET XER direct OPEN TYPE path with parent-aware selected
	  encoding, selector-first decoding, streaming replay, and malformed-input tests.
	* Add opt-in Rust CBOR codecs for BOOLEAN, NULL, bounded INTEGER and opaque
	  ANY with checked prefix decoding, resource limits and C parity vectors.
	* Add C SET CBOR direct IOC-selected OPEN TYPE dispatch with unordered-key
	  resolution, selected-arm storage validation, and cleanup of partial arms.
	* Extend the bounded Rust selected OPEN TYPE slice to OER and aligned APER,
	  with cumulative resource limits and C interoperability vectors.
	* Added C SET UPER OPEN TYPE roots and additions with deferred selectors,
	  nested-envelope checks, and generated SEQUENCE interoperability tests.
	* Generate a bounded UPER IOC-selected OPEN TYPE Rust slice with typed
	  variants, selector checks, shared resource limits and C parity tests.
	* Added C SET JER direct OPEN TYPE support with selector-order-independent
	  decoding, duplicate and selected-arm validation, and generated wire tests.
	* Validate C SET CBOR map members before encoding or decoding, reject
	  missing mandatory fields and duplicate known or unknown keys, and cover
	  all-optional SETs and malformed input in generated tests.
	* Check every present C SET member constraint, including later required and
	  OPTIONAL fields, and reject missing mandatory pointer fields. CER now
	  omits absent OPTIONAL ANY members in SEQUENCE and SET while continuing
	  to reject present opaque ANY values.
	* Reject malformed APER and OER SET OPEN TYPE members without a selector
	  before consuming input, except valid opaque APER fallback wrappers.
	* Validate selected OER OPEN TYPE descriptors and full storage spans, and
	  preserve preallocated values on failed envelope decoding. SET supports
	  the smaller inline ANY layout with validated parsing-context metadata.
	  Constructed children validate parser contexts, presence fields and list
	  storage before decoding or cleanup, with bounded cycle-aware validation
	  of constructed member tables and full storage slots.
	* Generate IOC-selected C SET members as open-type wrappers with selectors,
	  including pointer-backed extension IDs and additions. Selected OER values
	  must consume their complete envelope and retain inline arm constraints.
	* Added C SET APER and OER extension-addition OPEN TYPE encoding and
	  deferred decoding, including selectors in later additions and streaming
	  OER nested-envelope validation.
	* Adapted C ANY BER/DER, OER, CBOR, XER and JER byte handling to its
	  signed-size ABI, including bounds checks and safe buffer conversion.
	  Complete-value codec tests and split BER/JER decoding cover the adapters.
	* Added Rust UPER opaque ANY values as top-level assignments and required
	  or OPTIONAL SEQUENCE fields, with fragmented length handling, resource
	  limits, malformed-input tests, and generated C wire comparisons.
	  Direct ANY also supports APER, OER, and JER with C interoperability
	  vectors and malformed-input checks.
	* Added Rust UPER BIT/OCTET STRING CONTAINING a direct BOOLEAN or bounded
	  INTEGER at top level and in required or OPTIONAL SEQUENCE fields, with
	  shared cursor budgets, embedded-value validation, and C wire comparisons.
	* Promoted inline C BIT/OCTET STRING CONTAINING types into generated
	  descriptors, preserving INTEGER bounds and constructed-type metadata.
	  Marked contained descriptors as PDU-only generation dependencies and
	  added primitive, constructed, multi-module, and malformed-value tests.
	* Decode C SET APER and OER root OPEN TYPE fields after their table
	  selectors, including fields preceding selectors in canonical wire order.
	  OER retains deferred envelopes across incremental reads and frees them
	  when a partial SET is released.
	* Hardened C ANY APER and UPER decoding against malformed storage and
	  integer overflow, and fixed clearing APER conversion buffers.
	* Added C OCTET STRING (CONTAINING named Type) constraint checks for complete
	  embedded values. PER padding and spare values are validated, while
	  non-PER syntax uses complete-byte consumption. Added UPER and APER
	  negative cases to the CONTAINING smoke test. Syntax-aware recursive
	  constraint checks now have a depth bound.
	* Corrected C JER IOC-selected OPEN TYPE cleanup for incomplete and
	  malformed selected values. Added generated present/absent OPTIONAL
	  round trips, truncation and malformed-input regressions. JER text-string
	  decoding now rejects invalid JSON escapes, control bytes, and isolated
	  Unicode surrogates while accepting valid surrogate pairs.
	* Extended Rust UPER SEQUENCE fields to required and OPTIONAL inline
	  nonextensible ENUMERATED values, with C wire comparisons and malformed
	  rank tests. Unsupported Rust CONTAINING forms and IOC OPEN TYPE schemas
	  still fail before output publication while type resolution remains pending.
	* Encoded and decoded C SET extension-group leaves as flat JER object
	  members. Added key routing across input splits, duplicate and malformed
	  descriptor checks, DEFAULT and renamed-leaf regressions, and pretty
	  output. Group-bearing CBOR SET values now fail before output or decoder
	  allocation until a repository CBOR mapping is defined.
	* Added Rust JER encoding and decoding for direct bounded nonextensible
	  OCTET STRING values, with inclusive SIZE checks, malformed-input and
	  resource-limit tests, and generated C/Rust hexadecimal wire comparisons.
	* Added Rust JER encoding and decoding for direct fixed-size and bounded
	  BIT STRING values, with exact bit lengths, canonical padding checks,
	  resource limits, and generated C/Rust interoperability vectors.
	* Hardened C BIT STRING JER parsing and encoding for empty values,
	  malformed lengths, exact fixed sizes, unused-bit padding, and existing
	  value preservation on decode failure. C OCTET STRING JER hex and base64
	  encoders now handle null-backed empty values safely; base64 chunking no
	  longer narrows remaining lengths to int.
	* Added C UPER, APER, and OER support for SET extension groups. Version 3
	  metadata supplies a SEQUENCE wire view while preserving the synthetic SET
	  structure for other codecs. Groups use one addition bitmap bit and an
	  open type; empty or DEFAULT-only groups are omitted. Added independent
	  wire vectors, malformed-metadata tests, older-schema skipping, OER split
	  input, and single-flavor generated build checks.
	* Added generated Rust UPER encoding and decoding for nonextensible BIT
	  STRING values with one bounded SIZE range below 65536. A validated
	  packed value preserves exact bit length, including non-octet values.
	  Standalone and required or OPTIONAL SEQUENCE fields share bit cursors and
	  resource limits; generated C/Rust wire vectors and malformed-input tests
	  cover the new slice. Named-bit lists remain unsupported.
	* Added C OER encoding and streaming decoding for SETs with individual
	  extension additions. Versioned metadata separates roots from additions;
	  root values use canonical tag order and additions use declaration-order
	  open types. Known additions, unknown additions, DEFAULT restoration,
	  malformed bitmaps, split input, and extensible CHOICE ordering have
	  generated-code regressions. Legacy extensible descriptors continue to
	  fail closed.
	* Added generated Rust UPER encoding and decoding for OCTET STRING values
	  with one contiguous nonextensible SIZE range below 65536. Standalone
	  values and required or OPTIONAL SEQUENCE fields share checked bit cursors
	  and resource limits. Added malformed-length, unsupported-constraint,
	  strict Clippy, and generated C/Rust interoperability tests.
	* Added C APER encoding and decoding for SETs with individual extension
	  additions using versioned root and addition maps. Trailing roots retain
	  canonical tag order; known and unknown additions use aligned open types.
	  Added DEFAULT, truncation, malformed-metadata, and APER-only regressions.
	  Legacy extensible descriptors and extension groups remain unsupported.
	* Added generated Rust JER encoding and complete-input decoding for direct
	  fixed-size OCTET STRING values as quoted hexadecimal. Added uppercase
	  output, lowercase input, length and resource validation, malformed-input
	  tests, and two-way C interoperability vectors.
	* Added C UPER encoding and decoding for SETs with individual extension
	  additions. Versioned generated metadata records roots and additions,
	  including roots after a second marker. Decoding skips unknown additions
	  and preserves the open-type decoder status for truncated input. Legacy
	  extensible descriptors and extension groups fail closed in UPER.
	* Added generated Rust UPER support for inline nested SEQUENCE fields.
	  Required and OPTIONAL nested records share one bit cursor and resource
	  budget with their parent. Added C/Rust wire comparisons, nested DEFAULT
	  cases, and malformed-input and generator-limit regressions.
	* Corrected C OER table-selected open-type cleanup for incomplete and
	  failed CHOICE-wrapper decoding. Added ownership and malformed-input
	  regressions, including truncated length determinants.
	* Added literal BOOLEAN and bounded INTEGER DEFAULT fields to the
	  generated Rust flat SEQUENCE UPER slice. Presence bits share the
	  OPTIONAL bitmap, absent defaults are restored, and C wire interop
	  covers omitted and explicit-present default values. Direct component
	  tags, including AUTOMATIC TAGS, are accepted for UPER-only SEQUENCE.
	* Added C OER and APER encode/decode operations for nonextensible SET,
	  with canonical root tag order, optional/default presence handling,
	  streaming OER decode, APER member alignment, and generated-code
	  regressions. Extensible SET and table-selected open-type members
	  remain unsupported by these codecs.
	* Fixed C UPER SET ordering when an untagged CHOICE extension
	  alternative has a lower tag than its root alternatives. The
	  canonical root map now determines order; added a wire regression.
	* Added opt-in Rust JER encoding and strict complete-input decoding
	  for direct nonextensible ENUMERATED names, with generated-code and
	  malformed-input tests.
	* Added opt-in Rust JER encoding and complete-input decoding for direct
	  BOOLEAN, NULL, and finite bounded signed i64 INTEGER assignments.
	  The JSON primitives use compact tokens and enforce input, output, and
	  work limits. Added malformed-input and generated C/Rust comparison
	  tests. JER for other ASN.1 types remains pending.
	* Added UPER presence bitmaps for OPTIONAL direct fields in flat Rust
	  SEQUENCE assignments. Generated fields use Option<T>; present values
	  retain the shared cursor and resource budget. Added C wire comparisons
	  including a cross-octet presence bitmap, and negative DEFAULT,
	  nesting, extension, and tag regressions.
	* Kept BMPString__dump available in generated C JER-only builds where
	  print and XER support are disabled.
	* Added generated Rust UPER support for direct fixed-size OCTET STRING
	  and BIT STRING, standalone and as required flat SEQUENCE fields. The
	  runtime validates exact sizes and unused BIT STRING bits, packs fields
	  continuously, and enforces one complete-value resource budget. Added
	  generated-code and malformed-input regression tests.
	* Added direct nonextensible ENUMERATED UPER generation with root indexes
	  sorted by numeric value. Added spare-index, singleton, budget, and live
	  C interoperability regressions.
	* Added operation-wide UPER reader/writer budgets for composed fields and
	  generated Rust support for flat SEQUENCE assignments with required direct
	  BOOLEAN, NULL, and finite i64 INTEGER fields under UPER-only selection.
	  Each field charges its wire bits plus eight work units, including zero-bit
	  fields. Added packing, boundary, malformed-input, and budget regressions.
	* Added opt-in generated Rust APER and OER encoding/decoding for direct
	  BOOLEAN, NULL, and finite nonextensible signed i64 INTEGER assignments.
	  Added bounded runtime primitives, malformed-input and range-boundary
	  tests, generated API vectors, and offline packaging of both new modules.
	  Constructed and open types, and XER/JER, remain outside the Rust slice.
	* Extended the generated Rust primitive slice with opt-in BER decoding and
	  DER encoding for BOOLEAN, NULL, and bounded i64 INTEGER. BER accepts
	  definite long-form lengths and reports prefix consumption; DER emits
	  canonical primitive TLVs. Added malformed-input, resource-limit, and
	  generated-code regression coverage. The Rust default remains UPER/CER;
	  broader ASN.1 types and codec families remain pending. Rust CI now runs
	  pedantic and nursery Clippy lints with warnings denied.
	* Import standard ASN.1 modules in a deterministic order, keeping the
	  built-in EXTERNAL module first. Directory iteration order had shifted
	  generated descriptor indexes and failed check-parsing.sh in PR #593 CI.
	  Added a regression using opposite file creation orders.
	* Fixed issue #592: recursion-safe pointer members now name the defined
	  struct for numbered parameterized instances and constructed-type aliases.
	  Grow the generated tag buffer to fit long identifiers without truncation.
	  Added generated-header compile and long-name regressions.
	* Fixed issue #591: generate INTEGER DEFAULT setters and comparators
	  according to the actual selected C storage type. Unconstrained INTEGER
	  members in unsigned native modes now use INTEGER_t conversion callbacks
	  instead of invalid scalar operators. Added generated-code and callback
	  regressions for all integer-native storage modes. Encode negative DEFAULT
	  values with an identifier-safe "m" suffix in callback names.
	* Updated the 127-per-long compiler-output baseline after issue #590:
	  its two inline unsigned INTEGER members now reference their concrete
	  suffixed descriptors. This keeps check-parsing.sh aligned with generated
	  output and checks the corrected naming in the existing PER fixture.
	* Fixed issue #590: emit distinct suffixed descriptors for repeated,
	  constrained native INTEGER members nested in separate CHOICE alternatives
	  when compound names and fixed-width unsigned storage are enabled. Added a
	  generated-code compile/link regression for uint32 and uint64 modes.
	* Corrected callback error handling in JER UniversalString and canonical
	  XER SET OF encoders, and balanced JER CHOICE recursion depth when a child
	  encoder fails. Custom XER TEXT BIT STRING generation now omits callback
	  labels and callback-only variables when there are no named bits, so the
	  generated source compiles with strict warning settings. Added focused
	  failure-path and generated-code regressions.
	* Removed an unreachable XER SEQUENCE encoder failure label left after
	  callback handling moved into a helper; Apple Clang rejected the generated
	  code under -Wall -Werror. Pass the configured compiler to the IEEE 1609
	  IOC test so its generated-code build uses Clang in the Clang CI job.
	* Corrected the issue #552 C regression to inspect the alias descriptor's
	  inherited PER range instead of a generated constraint-table suffix, which
	  changes when symbol indexes are allocated across the input.
	* Fixed an infinite loop in generated constraint checkers exposed by
	  randomized OCTET STRING value-constraint tests. Recompute the generated
	  function name after constraint emission reuses the naming buffer, so
	  the recursion guard compares against the checker itself. Safely handle
	  an absent fallback callback. Regenerate affected C sources with the
	  updated compiler; existing generated binaries retain the faulty guard.
	* Corrected the check-65 multi-tag BER fixture: two binary REAL values
	  omitted their mantissas and were rejected after the issue #585 fix.
	  Use complete encodings and verify decoded values; retain missing-mantissa
	  inputs as rejection cases and cover truncation and malformed wrappers.
	* Fixed issue #586: retain unknown APER open-type payloads from extensible
	  information-object sets in a generated, owned ANY alternative, allowing
	  decode/modify/re-encode. Keep known alternatives' presence indices and
	  validate identifier/value agreement on encode. Reject unknown identifiers
	  in sealed sets. Correct optional open-type field declarations to match
	  pointer metadata. Regenerate C with the matching runtime; see
	  docs/issue-586-aper-unknown-open-type.md for framing and compatibility limits.
	  Correct ANY copy/compare/print to use its own structure layout, and CHOICE copy
	  to release a previous alternative safely when overwriting a populated value.
	  Free discarded NULL-placeholder extension allocations during APER decoding.
	  Added generated-code regressions and malformed/fragmented payload coverage.
	  Design and integration review by Sol; runtime and tests by Luna.
	* Fixed issue #585: BER binary REAL format 11 now consumes exactly the
	  explicit exponent octet count, accepting X=1 and avoiding mantissa
	  consumption for X=2/3. Reject missing exponents/mantissas and null result
	  pointers; preserve the existing ERANGE limit for X >= 4. Added raw and
	  NativeReal BER regressions, exact-buffer boundary checks, and a sweep of
	  all explicit length octets. See docs/issue-585-real-exponent.md for the
	  standards interpretation, permissive decoding scope, and validation.
	  Design and integration review by Sol; regression implementation by Luna.
	* Added transparent BER, DER, CER, and XER handling for SET extension
	  addition groups. Group leaves remain in a nested C allocation but encode
	  as independent members of the enclosing SET, with global canonical SET
	  ordering and required-member checks. CER applies the encoder's bounded
	  work, depth, element, and scratch limits while collecting flattened
	  members. Canonical XER sorts root members by their minimum effective tag,
	  then writes extension additions in textual order. It materializes grouped
	  DEFAULT members only when their group is present; ordinary SET defaults keep
	  their normal handling. Recursive SET XER decoding honors the configured
	  stack bound. The generated synthetic group is now a SET with
	  its own presence bitmap and mandatory mask, so regenerate generated C and
	  use the matching runtime.
	  SET extension-group PER support remains unavailable. The compiler also
	  restores trailing roots after a second ellipsis before tag assignment; the
	  31-set-of golden output covers this case. See docs/set-extension-groups.md.
	  Follow-up to issue #583, reported by Ruud Schramp (@Schramp). Architecture,
	  standards, and security review by Sol; runtime, test, fuzz, and documentation
	  implementation by Luna.
	* Fixed issues #582, #583 and #584 after validation against ITU-T X.680,
	  X.690, X.691 and X.693 (2021). Extensible FROM constraints now use the
	  built-in effective PER alphabet while abstract alphabet validation
	  separately enforces intersections, serial subtypes and EXCEPT. SEQUENCE
	  extension addition groups use flat BER/DER/CER/XER components and flat
	  automatic tags, retaining their C storage and PER open-type grouping.
	  EXTENSIBILITY IMPLIED now adds the ENUMERATED extension marker in its
	  defining module before numbering, including inline and imported types.
	  Regenerate generated C with the matching runtime: the SEQUENCE descriptor
	  interface has new group metadata. At that stage SET group encoding was
	  unchanged; transparent SET groups are covered by the follow-up above.
	  Reports by Ruud Schramp (@Schramp), cross-validated with the gambas-asn1
	  C++ and Rust backends with Claude Code assistance. Architecture, standards
	  and security review by asn1c maintainers with Codex/Sol; implementation,
	  regression tests, fuzzing and documentation with Codex/Luna assistance.
	* Security follow-up to #582-#584: fixed alphabet EXCEPT validation bypass,
	  malformed/incomplete BER group handling, DER SEQUENCE recursion-depth
	  cleanup and checked length accounting. Hardened OCTET STRING DER input
	  validation, including absent nonempty storage, invalid BIT STRING unused
	  bits and oversized lengths, and avoided null empty payload callbacks.
	  Made generated UniversalString character assembly use unsigned shifts
	  before validating high-bit input. Random string filling now respects PER
	  alphabet maps and abstract constraints, checks allocation bounds, and
	  preserves the prior value when bounded generation fails. Added malformed-
	  input, split-input, golden-vector, allocation-failure and sanitizer/fuzzer
	  coverage. See docs/issues-582-584-review.md for
	  standards references, validation results and review limitations.
	* Fixed the retagged-string randomized bundle's GCC UBSan failure when a
	  valid empty UTF8String reached OCTET_STRING_compare with a null backing
	  buffer. Empty comparisons/copies now avoid null C-library arguments;
	  hardened the corresponding BIT STRING operations and invalid copy-size
	  handling. Added deterministic empty tagged-string regressions alongside
	  the randomized cases. CI failure reported by the repository maintainer;
	  fixes and tests by asn1c maintainers with Codex/Luna assistance. This is
	  follow-up to the #578/#581 review; original reports by Ruud Schramp
	  (@Schramp).
	* Documented a proposed incremental JER design, covering per-PDU framing,
	  persistent typed decoding, limits, transactional sinks and split-input
	  testing against X.697/ECMA-404. This entry describes a proposal, not a
	  new streaming implementation. Motivated by issue #578 and PR #579 from
	  Ruud Schramp (@Schramp); design by asn1c maintainers with Codex assistance.
	* Verified the #578/#581 fixes against ITU-T X.680, X.690 and X.697
	  (2021), X.690 Erratum 1, and ECMA-404. The standards review found a
	  remaining fragment-validation gap in generated character-string aliases:
	  their final all_tags entry can still be the character-string tag.
	  Built-in component matching now enforces universal OCTET STRING tag 4
	  (or BIT STRING tag 3) below effective explicit wrappers, preserving ANY
	  and custom-operation behavior. Added alias-fragment regressions and
	  the published X.690 "Jones" examples. Corrected check-25's invalid
	  positive component tags while retaining all old tag forms as explicit
	  negative mutations; also covered all four JSON whitespace characters.
	  Standards review and follow-up correction by asn1c maintainers with
	  Codex/Luna assistance; original reporter and patch-provider credits
	  follow below.
	* Fixed issue #578: the JER converter now retains every PDU in large
	  concatenated inputs and checks decode failures instead of returning a
	  partial value as success. Replaced seek-based whole-file sizing with
	  checked stream buffering, including pipes; checked buffer growth and
	  released retained input before processing another file. Shared converter
	  handling now rejects read errors and impossible decoder consumption.
	  Added generated converter regressions for large/small multi-PDU inputs and malformed
	  input. Report and original PR #579 by Ruud Schramp (@Schramp), with
	  investigation assisted by Claude Code; security hardening and extended
	  tests by asn1c maintainers with Codex/Luna assistance.
	* Fixed issue #581 and completed PR #580: BER string wrapper checks use
	  the effective wire tag chain while fragment checks retain the descriptor's
	  final all_tags tag. The original PR changed the fragment fallback too,
	  accepting invalid VisibleString fragments and failing check-25 in all
	  three C CI jobs. Preserved that rejection test and added effective-tag,
	  malformed-fragment, generated-alias and randomized-string coverage.
	  Credits: Ruud Schramp (@Schramp) for issue #581 and its correct patch;
	  javier (@mr-j0nes) for PR #580 and the original skeleton regression;
	  asn1c maintainers with Codex/Luna assistance for security corrections
	  and extended regression coverage. See docs/issues-578-581-security-review.md.
	* Fixed PER security-review regressions in native unsigned 64-bit ranges:
	  APER/UPER now interpret both signed metadata slots as unsigned when the
	  type uses unsigned native storage, validate the complete range, and
	  reject invalid offsets before addition. Bounds above INTMAX_MAX work
	  without wrapping. Restored arbitrary-precision INTEGER (0..MAX)
	  decoding; native storage conversion still rejects values that do not fit.
	  Removed signed overflow in the APER encoder's full-range size calculation.
	  Added sanitized boundary, malformed/truncated-input and native-overflow
	  regressions, and generated uint64 coverage in the single-flavor smoke test.
	  Split PER INTEGER entry points into documented, bounded helpers, with
	  argument validation and checked fragmented-buffer growth.
	* Fixed builds generated with -no-gen-UPER (APER only). The PER range
	  helpers per_{long,imax,umax}_range_{rebase,unrebase}() used by both
	  INTEGER_aper.c and INTEGER_uper.c were defined only in uper_support.[ch],
	  which asn1c emits for the CODEC-UPER section alone. APER-only projects
	  therefore failed to compile with "call to undeclared function". The
	  helpers now live in per_support.[ch], which both CODEC-UPER and
	  CODEC-APER emit. -no-gen-UPER/-no-gen-APER still omit every file of
	  the disabled flavor. Added the check-PER-single-flavor.sh smoke test.
	  It builds APER-only and UPER-only converters, checks that no file of the
	  disabled flavor is emitted, round-trips constrained INTEGERs and checks
	  that the bytes match a combined build. This fixes the 17 asn1c-smoke
	  failures.
	* Added a strict C CER decoder, cer_decode(), which runs ber_decode(),
	  re-encodes the value with cer_encode(), and rejects input (EBADF) that
	  is not byte-identical to the consumed TLV. asn_decode(ATS_CER) and the
	  generated converter's -icer now use it; ATS_BER and ATS_DER remain
	  permissive. -icer requires CER generation, is rejected under
	  -no-gen-CER, and buffers the whole input. ASN_DISABLE_BER_SUPPORT or
	  ASN_DISABLE_CER_SUPPORT builds a stub failing with ENOENT. The Rust
	  runtime adds strict decode_boolean_cer, decode_null_cer, and
	  decode_integer_cer, and generated Rust types emit decode_cer alongside
	  encode_cer whenever CER is selected. Added skeleton, smoke, and Rust
	  runtime/interop regressions, including live C-generated CER vectors.
	* Skip unused randomized corpus generation when LibFuzzer is disabled.
	  Added GENERATE_CORPUS=auto/yes/no and a local-only check-corpus target
	  that splits bundles into parallel cases without timed fuzzing. Inner
	  builds share the caller's job budget. Corpus/fuzz success markers are
	  separate, and policy/failure regressions run in the ordinary checks.
	* Corrected CER restricted-character-string fragments to use universal
	  OCTET STRING tags, preserving the outer string type tag. BER decoding
	  no longer accepts a character-type tag in a nested OCTET STRING-only
	  fragment position. Restored legacy opaque ANY container compatibility
	  without removing parent-length, nesting, or EOC validation. Added fixed
	  byte-vector and malformed/streaming regressions for generated C tests
	  25, 60, and 62; randomized corruption coverage is retained.
	  All 71 generated C checks and 52 linked skeleton checks pass, along
	  with CER codec-disable variants and Rust/C interoperability checks.
	* Added --rust as a complete output mode with native safe Rust UPER
	  encode/decode and CER encoding for BOOLEAN, NULL, and finite
	  nonextensible INTEGER ranges fitting i64. Generated Cargo packages use
	  a dependency-free Rust runtime. Rust CER is encode-only; other Rust
	  codecs and ASN.1 type families remain incremental conversion work.
	* Added a native descriptor-driven C CER encoder, exposed through
	  cer_encode(), the generic ATS_CER encoder, and generated converter
	  output. C CER support is enabled by default with BER dependencies. CER
	  input still uses permissive BER decoding. Added string fragmentation,
	  constructed values, SET/SET OF ordering, malformed-input, and converter
	  regression coverage. Primitive content capture uses a single intrinsic tag;
	  the descriptor walker reapplies wrappers under the configurable tag-chain
	  limit. Existing BER corpora also feed decoded values to generic CER encoding
	  in randomized tests; this is not a long fuzz run.
	* Extended BER-family CER input handling for explicit/named wrappers,
	  natural-tag string fragments, and definite constructed BER children for
	  covered tagged scalar forms. Validated NativeInteger width/sign metadata
	  while preserving default native storage and DEFAULT omission. Mixed lengths
	  among nested constructed scalar wrappers remain limited by the existing
	  BER tag-chain path. The corrected encoder passes the linked skeleton suite
	  (52/52), and the Rust harness passes all 10 conformance checks with C parity.
	  A short ASan/UBSan run passes 660,325 mutations. The generated CER converter
	  script, all 28 generated smoke tests, and installed-toolchain qualification
	  pass.
	* Documented the proposed first stage of Rust conversion: an opt-in Rust
	  generation backend, a safe Rust runtime for all current codec families,
	  test migration, and supervised implementation milestones. This change
	  initially added planning documentation; the first implementation is
	  described above.
	* Fixed an assertion when parsing nested constrained SEQUENCE OF and SET OF
	  types. Element constraints now pass through nested collections while SIZE
	  constraints remain attached to their collections. Added issue #575 coverage.
	* Constraint checks now enforce SIZE bounds on constrained SEQUENCE OF and
	  SET OF values, including collections nested in other types. The generated
	  checker still validates each element. Added issue #570 regression coverage.
	* The contents constraint (BIT STRING (CONTAINING Type), X.682 clause 11)
	  is no longer ignored. The generated constraint check (-c) rejects
	  content that does not decode as Type using the selected transfer syntax
	  (BER by default), and the random generator (-R) encodes a random Type
	  value using the selected output syntax. Adds syntax-aware variants of
	  the constraint-checking and random-fill APIs, and the contained_type
	  field of asn_encoding_constraints_t. OCTET STRING (CONTAINING Type) is
	  not yet covered. Added issue #569 regression coverage.
	* Fixed default tag-mode resolution for tagged SEQUENCE OF and SET OF
	  elements. References to already-tagged CHOICE types now use IMPLICIT
	  tagging, as required by X.680:2021 §31.2.7. Added issue #566 regression
	  coverage for normalized ASN.1 and generated member descriptors.
	* Corrected primitive runtime file dependencies for BER, XER, and JER when
	  using -fgen-only-pdu-deps, so generated projects include required shared
	  codec helpers. Added isolated dependency-generation regression coverage.
	* BER SEQUENCE decoding now rejects a first unknown extension addition
	  whose tag duplicates a trailing OPTIONAL or DEFAULT root component tag,
	  as required by X.680:2021 §§25.6 and 52.7. Added issue #213 regression
	  coverage.
	* Added a repository code-review guide for contributors.

v1.5.3: 2026-10-07
	* Corrected IMPORTS resolution and diagnostics. Explicitly imported names
	  resolve from the module named by FROM; -fprefer-import-source disables
	  the legacy whole-module fallback. Duplicate module references are
	  diagnosed, OID equality checks avoid treating name-form arcs as numbers,
	  parameterized imported types avoid spurious diagnostics, and all FATAL
	  diagnostics produce a non-zero exit status. Added compiler regression
	  coverage (PR #560 follow-up).
	* Fixed PER extensibility handling for information-object identifier fields
	  governed by object sets and for component-relation constraints. Recovery
	  is limited to table-only constraints where appropriate. Added UPER and
	  APER regression coverage for issue #563 (PR #564).
	* Fixed a parallel uninstall race in the skeleton build that could cause
	  make distcheck to fail (PR #564).
	* Prevented generated filenames from colliding with skeleton files on
	  case-insensitive filesystems by disambiguating matching names with an
	  asn1c_ prefix. Added a smoke test and documentation.
	* Moved constraint enums to file scope and made asn1p_constr.h
	  self-contained, so C++-based code analyzers can parse the declarations.
	* Updated and regenerated the usage guide and man page to match current
	  behavior, including the transfer-syntax API table and groff rendering.
	  Added Markdown lint and VS Code workspace settings.

Changes since v1.5.0:
	* Made the generated-constraint warning regression test compatible with
	  Automake's standard top_srcdir/top_builddir test environment.
	* Avoided redundant parentheses around standalone equality comparisons in
	  generated constraint checks, preventing Clang's -Wparentheses-equality
	  warning while retaining required grouping for compound expressions.
	* Hardened APER open-type decoding against undefined NULL-pointer arithmetic
	  when malformed input begins with a zero-length chunk.  Regression coverage
	  now exercises the corresponding aligned-PER vector in check-126.
	  Fix suggested by <shakespark@gmail.com> in <https://github.com/vlm/asn1c/pull/551>.
	* Generalized generated OER, UPER, and APER descriptor constraint-table
	  inheritance for typedef aliases by deriving codec slots from the terminal
	  ASN.1 type.
	  Issue #552, reported by @zhouvlia, was already avoided for ENUMERATED aliases
	  by an earlier enum-specific branch in this fork; the new terminal-type rule
	  covers the remaining alias classes and the added UPER/APER regression locks
	  in the reported behavior and truncation safety.
	* Corrected generated UPER/APER CHOICE maps so conversions between declaration
	  order and canonical order use the right direction. Added canonical-order
	  regression coverage in check-561. Fix in PR #562, included in v1.5.2.
	  Problem and fix provided by Ruud Schramp.
	IMPORTANT UPGRADE NOTICE:
	* Decoding behavior for unknown extensions has changed from "fail" to
	  "skip/relay". Evaluate the impact on your application before upgrading;
	  define ASN_REJECT_UNKNOWN_EXTENSIONS when compiling the decoder skeletons
	  to restore the previous strict behavior. This change can affect input-
	  validation gates and protocol state machines that treated RC_FAIL as a
	  protocol error.
	  Compatibility warning contributed by <shakespark@gmail.com>.

	INTEROPERABILITY FIXES (vlm/asn1c PRs #539-#548 and #550):
	* Co-authored-by: libo <shakespark@gmail.com>
	* The original fixes were authored by @shakespark (this notice is placed
	  here upon his request).
	* Ported vlm/asn1c PR #550 so generated permitted-alphabet constraint
	  checks accept a buffer-less empty string without NULL-pointer arithmetic
	  and deterministically reject malformed values whose buffer is NULL while
	  their size is non-zero. Runtime regression coverage exercises both empty
	  representations plus malformed, in-alphabet, and out-of-alphabet values;
	  generated permitted-alphabet helpers now include complete doc-blocks.
	* Corrected UPER known-multiplier character strings with extensible SIZE
	  constraints to retain their effective permitted-alphabet width outside
	  the size root, as required by X.691:2021 sections 30.4 and 30.5.2.
	  Also corrected the section 30.5.4 direct-value boundary, supported
	  zero-bit single-character alphabets, and rejected length arithmetic
	  overflow before allocation. Regression test 550 covers exact root and
	  extension encodings, round trips, malformed alphabet values, forward
	  decoding, empty strings, and a following-field cursor check.
	* Corrected UPER/OER forward-compatible handling of unknown CHOICE and
	  ENUMERATED extensions, including lossless ENUMERATED relay and the
	  optional ASN_REJECT_UNKNOWN_EXTENSIONS strict compatibility mode.
	* Corrected UPER normally-small long-form encoding, extensible constraint
	  construction, DEFAULT extension omission, SET canonical ordering, and
	  ENUMERATED automatic numbering/map layout.
	* Corrected OER open-type skipping to consume both its length determinant
	  and content, and added regression schemas and runtime tests for malformed,
	  truncated, boundary, cross-version, and canonical-encoding cases.
	* PR #539's 24-bit open-type skip defect was not present in this fork: its
	  existing bit-at-a-time skipper already consumed every payload length. The
	  upstream regression test was retained to lock in that behavior.
	* Fixed codec-disabled builds of NativeEnumerated by applying the UPER
	  extension-range consistency check only when the UPER limit constant is
	  available. This restores the all-codecs-disabled smoke-test variant.
	* Fixed generated UPER projects to include constr_SET_uper.c, and hardened
	  non-empty SET OF / SEQUENCE OF decoding against missing element codecs.
	  Empty collections remain valid because they do not invoke an element
	  codec.
	* Corrected PER-visible extensible SIZE roots so named extension additions
	  are excluded from the root while remaining accepted by runtime constraint
	  checks. Plain BIT STRING values below an extensible root are encoded as
	  extensions instead of being padded into a different abstract value.
	* Routed NamedBitList-specific BIT STRING descriptors through top-level
	  aliases and inline members, including compound-name output, while plain
	  BIT STRING values continue to preserve trailing zero bits.

	SECURITY FIXES:
	* Hardened APER constrained INTEGER decoding for ranges wider than 16 bits.
	  The decoder now rejects constraint metadata wider than its uintmax_t
	  accumulator and invalid values from the rounded constrained length
	  determinant before alignment or payload consumption.  Offset accumulation
	  remains unsigned and checks for shift overflow, preventing signed-shift
	  undefined behavior and over-long encodings that could desynchronize later
	  fields.  Added regression coverage for the reported 33-bit/8-octet input
	  and the 64-bit boundary path.
	* Hardened variable-size JER BIT STRING decoding.  The decoder now requires
	  the X.697 "value" and "length" members exactly once, rejects unknown or
	  trailing members, and does not assign a first- or last-member winner to
	  duplicate JSON names.  This prevents duplicate-member parser differentials
	  from silently changing the decoded bit string across implementations.
	  X.697 clause 24.3 defines the two required members but does not define a
	  duplicate-name resolution rule; RFC 8259 section 4 recommends unique names
	  and documents duplicate-name behavior as unpredictable.
	* Fixed generated OPEN TYPE selector code for Information Object Sets
	  whose rows define the selected open type but omit the constraining
	  key field.  The generated selector now validates both the constraining
	  cell and selected type cell before dereferencing type descriptors or
	  compare callbacks, preventing NULL dereferences on malicious input.
	  OPEN TYPE encoder and printer paths were also hardened to reject NULL
	  selected descriptors before debug logging, encoding, or printing.
	  Regression test 211 now covers the crash packet pattern and
	  BER/DER/OER/UPER/APER/XER/JER/CBOR round trips plus plaintext
	  printing through the same selector edge case.
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: low)
	* Hardened CVE-2025-32893 handling for parameterized Information Object
	  Sets by safely comparing VALUESET constraint references without
	  dereferencing optional constraint fields, and added regression test 212
	  to verify distinct value sets produce distinct open-type validation.
	  (Severity: medium; Security impact: medium)
	* Fixed CBOR unknown-field skipping so recursive arrays, maps, and tags
	  are covered by the decoder stack limit.  SEQUENCE and SET decoders use
	  the new cbor_skip_item_with_ctx() helper when skipping unknown CBOR
	  map values; the original cbor_skip_item() remains as a compatibility
	  wrapper for callers without decoder context.  Added check-CBOR
	  regression coverage for deeply nested tag wrappers.
	  (Severity: medium; Security impact: low)
	* Fixed BER CHOICE decoding infinite loop on malformed indefinite-length
	  end-of-contents (CWE-835, DoS on attacker-controlled input).  A leading
	  0x00 byte followed by a non-zero byte fell through an unhandled branch
	  in constr_CHOICE_ber.c without returning or advancing the buffer,
	  causing the decoder to spin forever.  The missing branch now returns
	  RC_FAIL, matching constr_SEQUENCE_ber.c / constr_SET_ber.c /
	  constr_SET_OF_ber.c behavior.  Added regression test
	  (203-ber-indef-loop-OK.asn1, check-203.c) covering all four
	  indefinite-length BER decoders, plus a libFuzzer harness and seed
	  corpus (data-203).  Ported from upstream vlm/asn1c PR #518; originally
	  reported by John Bradley (Credex).
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: low)

	FIXES:
	* Reduced randomized sanitizer CI compile time by applying each case's
	  ASN1_TEXT definition only to random-test-driver.o. Shared generated codec
	  objects now have stable command lines that ccache can reuse across bundle
	  cases. Standard CI explicitly disables the opt-in LibFuzzer mode and caps
	  every ordinary CI job, as well as each make-check step, at 40 minutes.
	* Restored the X.691 section 13.2.6 constrained length determinant
	  for APER constrained INTEGER values whose range is greater than
	  65536.  A previous fix for wide INTEGER constraint handling changed
	  this path to the general APER length determinant, producing and
	  expecting non-conformant encodings such as 01 20 instead of 00 20
	  for INTEGER (0..4294967295) ::= 32.  The decoder and encoder now
	  use the constrained len-1 bit field followed by octet alignment
	  while preserving the unsigned offset accumulation and negative lower
	  bound checks needed for 64-bit ranges.
	* Fixed tests/tests-asn1c-compiler subdirectory checks so they build
	  asn1c before running scripts that invoke it.  This prevents
	  check-parsing.sh from comparing references against empty output when
	  the compiler has not already been built by a top-level make.
	* Fixed Darwin libtool configuration when `sysctl -n kern.argmax` is
	  denied by the host environment.  configure now seeds libtool's command
	  line length cache from `getconf ARG_MAX`, avoiding empty max_cmd_len
	  values and noisy "integer expression expected" diagnostics while
	  linking skeleton archives.
	* Ported upstream OPEN TYPE and option validation fixes.  Decoders now
	  reject information object rows whose selector has no type descriptor
	  instead of dereferencing NULL, and OER OPEN TYPE failure cleanup resets
	  the OPEN TYPE CHOICE wrapper instead of using the selected primitive
	  type size.  Added regression test 211 for typeless information object
	  rows and truncated OPEN TYPE payloads.  The compiler now rejects
	  -fno-constraints with -gen-OER, -gen-UPER, or -gen-APER because those
	  encoders/decoders require constraint metadata.
	* Fixed additional fuzzer-discovered decoder issues:
	  - JER BIT STRING now rejects invalid length metadata instead of
	    accepting lengths larger than the decoded bit buffer or with more
	    than seven unused bits.
	  - APER SEQUENCE frees extension presence maps on starvation paths.
	  - APER NativeReal and OCTET STRING reject malformed length/range
	    cases found by fuzzing.
	  - JER and XER SET OF decoding now treats zero-progress member decodes
	    as failure, preventing loops on malformed input.
	  - The JER decoder and randomized/fuzzer test runners now handle
	    malformed or truncated inputs without writing discoveries back into
	    source-tree corpora.
	* Fixed XER OCTET STRING entity-reference handling so Unicode U+0000 is
	  accepted while out-of-range and surrogate numeric character references
	  fail cleanly with a terminated working buffer.
	* Keyed the single definition of `asn_debug_indent` in asn_internal.c
	  off a macro (ASN__DEBUG_INDENT_NEEDS_DEFINITION) set by asn_internal.h
	  under exactly the configuration which declares the variable extern.
	  Previously the definition's guard did not account for an external
	  ASN_DEBUG override, so building with -DASN_EMIT_DEBUG=1 plus a custom
	  -DASN_DEBUG=... failed to compile asn_internal.c.  Aligned with
	  upstream vlm/asn1c PR #520.
	* tests: instrument generated codec libraries with libFuzzer coverage
	  counters (-fsanitize=fuzzer-no-link) so fuzzing gets feedback from the
	  ASN.1 codec itself, and seed fuzzer runs from a scratch corpus copy so
	  discoveries are not written back into the source tree.  Ported from
	  upstream vlm/asn1c PR #518.

	NEW FEATURES:
	* Added schema-level XER/JER encoding instruction support for the
	  implemented subset of X.693/X.697-style controls.  The parser now
	  accepts `JER INSTRUCTIONS`, `[TEXT]`, `[XER:TEXT]`, `[DECIMAL]`,
	  `[XER:DECIMAL]`, `[JER:BASE64]`, `ENCODING-CONTROL XER` directives
	  for `TEXT`, `DECIMAL`, and `GLOBAL-DEFAULTS MODIFIED-ENCODINGS`, and
	  `ENCODING-CONTROL JER` directives for `BASE64`, enumerated-value
	  `TEXT AS`, and member `NAME AS`.
	  - Added semantic validation for target applicability, unknown targets,
	    required `AS` values, XER `DECIMAL` requiring
	    `GLOBAL-DEFAULTS MODIFIED-ENCODINGS`, and duplicate JER wire names.
	  - Added generated XER text wrappers for BOOLEAN, ENUMERATED,
	    named-number INTEGER, and named-bit BIT STRING; XER decimal REAL
	    routing; JER Base64 OCTET STRING wrappers; and JER member wire-name
	    metadata used by SEQUENCE, SET, and CHOICE encoders/decoders.
	  - Preserved compatibility for bare `[BASE64]` as XER and the legacy
	    XER OCTET STRING `hexadecimal`, `base64`, and `utf8` control forms.
	  - Added compiler golden and smoke tests covering allowed forms, bad
	    values, bad applicability, exact XER/JER output, JER round trips, and
	    JER bad-wire failures.
	* Added `-fprefer-import-source` compiler flag.  When two modules export
	  identically-named types and a consumer imports one from each,
	  `asn1f_lookup_in_imports` previously fell back to a full-module body
	  scan and silently bound to the wrong module's definition.  With
	  `-fprefer-import-source` the resolver only accepts an explicit
	  IMPORTS-list match, eliminating the ambiguity.  The fix also corrects
	  flag propagation through `_ex` wrapper functions and across the
	  `memset` that clears `a1f_replace_me_with_proper_interface_arg`, so
	  compiler-phase lookups now correctly inherit caller-supplied flags.

1.3.6:
	FIXES:
	* Initialize `char ch` before taking its address in
	  asn_codecs_prim_xer.c and asn_codecs_prim_jer.c to silence
	  clang -Werror,-Wuninitialized-const-pointer. Reported by ur20980.

1.3.5:
	FIXES:
	* Prevent unsigned underflow in APER constrained INTEGER decoding when
	  reading length-octets for ranges wider than 16 bits. The decoder now
	  rejects zero-length determinants and avoids size_t wraparound flagged
	  by UBSan on macOS builds. Reported by mouse07410.
	* Fixed check-fprefix-link.sh smoke test to ensure proper option
	  ordering for macOS compatibility. The test now places all command-line
	  options before the input file, avoiding POSIX getopt() behavior where
	  option processing stops at the first non-option argument.

1.3.4:
	NEW FEATURES:
	* Added CBOR tag support (RFC 8949 §3.4, major type 6).
	  - All CBOR decoders are now tag-transparent: any number of leading
	    tag headers are silently skipped before decoding the underlying
	    value.  Tagged data from external producers (self-described CBOR
	    tag 55799, epoch timestamps tag 1, URI hints tag 32, etc.) is
	    accepted without application-level changes.
	  - New cbor_skip_tags() helper in cbor_support.[ch] peels off
	    consecutive leading CBOR tag headers from a raw buffer.
	  - Added well-known CBOR tag constants to cbor_support.h:
	    CBOR_TAG_DATETIME_STRING (0), CBOR_TAG_EPOCH_DATETIME (1),
	    CBOR_TAG_DECIMAL_FRACTION (4), CBOR_TAG_BIGFLOAT (5),
	    CBOR_TAG_BASE64URL (21), CBOR_TAG_BASE64 (22), CBOR_TAG_BASE16 (23),
	    CBOR_TAG_ENCODED_CBOR (24), CBOR_TAG_URI (32), CBOR_TAG_REGEX (35),
	    CBOR_TAG_UUID (37), CBOR_TAG_NETWORK_ADDR (260),
	    CBOR_TAG_SELF_DESCRIBED (55799).
	  - Extended check-CBOR test suite with comprehensive tag tests:
	    cbor_encode_tag() output verification, cbor_skip_tags() unit tests,
	    tag-transparent decode tests for INTEGER, OCTET STRING, NativeInteger,
	    and BIT STRING types, and nested multi-tag decode tests.
	  - Updated asn1c-usage.tex: added "CBOR Tags" API section documenting
	    encoding with cbor_encode_tag(), tag-transparent decoding, and
	    bignum tags. Added IANA CBOR Tags Registry reference.
	    Updated CBOR references from RFC 7049 to RFC 8949 (successor).
	  - Updated asn1c.man.md: added CBOR TAGS section and updated RFC
	    reference from RFC 7049 to RFC 8949.
	FIXES:
	* Fixed generated filename collisions with system headers on
	  case-insensitive filesystems (notably macOS/Windows). ASN.1 types
	  whose generated filenames match common system headers are now
	  disambiguated automatically (e.g., Time.h -> asn1c_time.h),
	  preventing accidental inclusion of generated headers when source
	  files include <time.h>. Added smoke-test coverage for the Time case.

1.3.3:
	NEW FEATURES:
	* Added complete CBOR (Concise Binary Object Representation, RFC 7049)
	  codec support. CBOR generation is enabled by default; use -no-gen-CBOR
	  to disable. New skeleton files: cbor_encoder.[ch], cbor_decoder.[ch],
	  cbor_support.[ch], INTEGER_cbor.c, NativeInteger_cbor.c,
	  OCTET_STRING_cbor.c, BIT_STRING_cbor.c, BOOLEAN_cbor.c, NULL_cbor.c,
	  ENUMERATED_cbor.c, NativeEnumerated_cbor.c, REAL_cbor.c,
	  NativeReal_cbor.c, constr_SEQUENCE_cbor.c, constr_SEQUENCE_OF_cbor.c,
	  constr_SET_cbor.c, constr_SET_OF_cbor.c, constr_CHOICE_cbor.c,
	  asn_codecs_prim_cbor.c. The SEQUENCE encoder correctly skips absent
	  optional and default-valued members so the CBOR map header count always
	  matches the number of encoded key/value pairs. INTEGER decoding handles
	  CBOR bignum tags (2 and 3) for values exceeding the 64-bit signed range.
	  New test: tests/tests-skeletons/check-CBOR.c with edge-case coverage for
	  INTEGER, NativeInteger, BIT STRING, and OCTET STRING types.
	* Added ATS_CBOR to asn_transfer_syntax enum and wired CBOR encode/decode
	  into asn_encode()/asn_decode() dispatch in asn_application.c. Added
	  -icbor and -ocbor switches to converter-example.c so that generated
	  converter applications can read and write CBOR-encoded data.

1.3.2:
	FIXES:
	* Fixed incorrect type descriptor selection when the same member name appears
	  in different parent types with different type definitions. When embedded types
	  like ssb-PositionsInBurst appeared as CHOICE in one parent and SEQUENCE in
	  another, the decoder would incorrectly use the wrong type descriptor due to
	  unsuffixed alias collisions at runtime. The fix ensures member table references
	  always use suffixed type descriptors for embedded constructed types, avoiding
	  ambiguity. Affects 3GPP RRC and similar specifications with duplicate member
	  names across different parent structures.
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Moved complex_threshold from global variable to arg_t structure field.
	  Applications linking to libasn1compiler no longer need to define their own
	  version of the global complex_threshold variable. The variable is now properly
	  encapsulated within the compiler's argument structure and passed through the
	  asn1_compile() function. Default threshold value remains 4. Added test case
	  for -fcomplex-threshold flag validation.
	  (Severity: low; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed JER OPEN TYPE decoder to comply with ITU-T X.697 Clause 41. The decoder
	  was incorrectly attempting to parse CHOICE-style key wrappers and consuming
	  parent SEQUENCE delimiters, causing "Unexpected JSON key" and "Out of defined
	  members" errors when decoding valid ITU-T X.697 compliant JSON. The decoder now
	  decodes OPEN TYPE values directly without wrapper parsing and returns immediately
	  without consuming trailing delimiters, letting parent decoders handle structural
	  elements. Added automated regression test to prevent future issues. Affects F1AP
	  and similar specifications with OPEN TYPE fields. (PR #456)
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: none)

1.3.1:
	FEATURES:
	* Enhanced -fprefix implementation with automatic PDU handling and system
	  header conflict warnings. (PR #427)
	* Added warning system to detect filename conflicts with system headers on
	  case-insensitive filesystems. (PR #425)

	NOTABLE:
	* Added S1AP missing ASN.1 file to examples. (PR #423)

	FIXES:
	* Improved JER OPEN_TYPE encoder validation and diagnostics. Added comprehensive
	  checks for type descriptor validity, NULL pointer detection, and type mismatch
	  warnings. Enhanced debug logging to help diagnose encoding issues in complex
	  IOC scenarios. (Severity: low; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed name collision for nested CHOICE/SET members with identical identifiers.
	  When the same identifier appears recursively in nested CHOICE or SET structures
	  (e.g., "criticalExtensions" used at multiple nesting levels in 3GPP RRC schemas),
	  the compiler now automatically applies compound naming to prevent collisions.
	  This fixes UPER decoding failures in 3GPP WCDMA RRC and similar schemas.
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed JER Open Type encoding to comply with ITU-T X.697 Clause 41 - removed
	  incorrect type name wrapper. (PR #444) (Severity: medium; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed SEQUENCE OF with inline SEQUENCE inside CHOICE generating undefined
	  types. (PR #442) (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed linker errors from duplicate unsuffixed type descriptor symbols on
	  non-ELF platforms (CYGWIN, Windows). (PR #439) (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed duplicate validation function names for nested ENUMERATEDs with
	  identical identifiers. (PR #436) (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed parser memory leak on syntax error. (PR #434) (Severity: low; Security impact: low)
	* Fixed memory leak in parser when processing unused tokens. (PR #433)
	  (Severity: low; Security impact: low)
	* Fixed code generation for deeply nested SEQUENCE OF with compound names.
	  (PR #432) (Severity: medium; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed XER Base64 decoder state loss in chunked decoding. (PR #430)
	  (Severity: medium; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed time.h shadowing on case-insensitive filesystems (macOS, Windows) by
	  moving include to header files. (PR #425) (Severity: medium; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed XER encoder indentation and empty element spacing issues. (PR #420)
	  (Severity: low; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed unused variable 'er' in OPEN_TYPE_jer.c that caused compilation
	  failure with -Werror -Wall flags. (Severity: low; Security impact: none)

